+/* A Rietveld refinement that goes on in the tab left (backlog 23, option A): leaving its tab
+   asks nothing; the run, detached from its card, writes each result into the tab's parked
+   state (and the database: a reload keeps them), the tab unsaved, a spinner on it; its end
+   goes into the parked history as a live run's does (one step, after the state it started
+   from); the tab shown again, its card takes the run back (Cancel, progress, rows locked)
+   or shows it ended. Two tabs refining at once, a third on show. Closing the parked tab
+   asks, then stops it; deleting its project stops it; the Projects list exports what is
+   saved; Save from the close saves what was written so far. Refine the standard first,
+   left at once: both runs go on, a step each, in order. The workers' answers are held
+   (window.__hold) so that a run goes as far as the test needs. */
+import { test, before, after } from 'node:test';
